Version 7.1

10/15/26  [GH #307]
Suppress the blocks macros in make_predef_macro_table output

The __BLOCKS__ and __block macros are now suppressed when running
make_predef_macro_table with --clang (so these don't end up in a
predefined_macros.txt file).  Clang defines them together when the blocks
extension is enabled (the default for Apple clang), but the front end does not
support that extension, and the system headers that test __BLOCKS__ (the macOS
SDK declares atexit_b, qsort_b and others under it) would then use block
pointer types.  They have also been removed from the predefined_macros.txt
files of the macOS clang bases.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 7.0, September 28, 2026

9/27/26  [EDGcpfe/29061]

mk_errinfo could produce incorrect output (e.g., missing font changes)
when the -rst option was used.  Now fixed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 6.9, July 20, 2026

8/25/26  [EDGcpfe/29018]
Use a standard shebang line in make_predef_macro_table

The make_predef_macro_table script previously did not use a standard POSIX
shebang line; this is now fixed.


6/29/26  [EDGcpfe/28929]
Spaces are improperly processed on various options

Previously, various options (like --sys_include) did not properly quote
their arguments, resulting in arguments unintentionally decaying into multiple
arguments (if the argument contained a space).  This is now fixed.


5/14/26  [EDGcpfe/28833]
Demangled names for fabricated field names of base objects

The front end creates fabricated names for some field names in lowered
classes.  The demangler has been updated to provide demangled names for
such fields.  This change is for both the IA-64 and Cfront ABIs.


3/4/26   [EDGcpfe/28581]
reStructuredText output from mk_errinfo

In addition to LaTeX and Maker Markup Language (Adobe FrameMaker) formats,
mk_errinfo now also supports reStructuredText (see
https://docutils.sourceforge.io/rst.html) when creating a human-readable
summary description of the front end's diagnostic messages for inclusion in
the front end documentation.  For example,

  mk_errinfo -rst error_msg.txt error_tag.txt err_msgs.rst


