Version 6.4, October 25, 2022

10/14/22 [EDGcpfe/25681]
Improve dettarg setjmp and jmp_buf deduction support

dettarg now supports calculating JMP_BUF definitions for jmp_buf
implementations that are not based on arrays of integer types.

Additionally, dettarg now properly supports libraries that remap "setjmp" to a
different underlying function via a macro.  As an example, libstdc++ (at the
time of writing) has switched to define setjmp as:

  #define setjmp(env) _setjmp(env)

where _setjmp is the actual function EDG should be calling.


9/30/22  [EDGcpfe/20094,EDGcpfe/20264,EDGcpfe/25494]
GNU/Clang compatibility: _Float16

Demangling now supports the _Float16 16-bit floating-point type.


1/21/22  [EDGcpfe/25004]
IA-64 ABI demangling issue

IA-64 ABI mangled names that contain a two-character substitution followed by a
name that begins with "_I" had been improperly demangled.  For example,
_ZSt9_Is_slash had been demangled as "std(_Is_slash)" and is now properly
demangled as "std::_Is_slash".


1/3/22   [EDGcpfe/24962]
Rename a_substitution struct

In some cases, the a_substitution struct in decode.c could conflict with a
similarly named struct in lower_name.c.  To avoid such a collision the one
in decode.c has now been renamed a_substitution_location.


