9/21/20  [EDGcpfe/23362]
Demangling for designated initializers

Following the implementation of designated initializer mangling in the
front end, support has been added for demangling names with designated
initializer mangling.  The Cfront ABI uses the same mangling structure as
the IA-64 ABI.


8/7/20   [EDGcpfe/23225]
Options for --[no_]utf8_char_literals

The options controlling support for UTF-8 character literals (see
EDGcpfe/16385) were inadvertently omitted from eccp.  This is now fixed.


8/3/20   [EDGcpfe/20033,EDGcpfe/20276,EDGcpfe/22245]
Demangling for template parameter objects

As a result of the changes for nontype template parameters of class type or
floating-point type (a C++20 feature), demangling has been added for template
parameter objects.  The IA-64 ABI has not been officially updated to reflect
these changes but GCC uses "TA" for these objects and these are now properly
decoded.  The Cfront ABI uses "__TPO__".


