6/29/20  [EDGcpfe/23022]
Demangling for spaceship operator

Demangling for the spaceship (<=>) operator has been added for both the
IA-64 and Cfront configurations.


4/14/20  [EDGcpfe/22614]
Have dettarg consider long long integer types

The dettarg program determines various host-specific configuration
information for use in configuring the front end.  Previously the "long long"
integer type had not been considered as a possible integer type for various
types (e.g., size_t) and is now (when HAVE_LONG_LONG is TRUE).


3/16/20  [EDGcpfe/17687]
IA-64 ABI: Demangling for inheriting constructors

Demangling for inheriting constructors (see the Changes entry in the src
directory) has now been added.  Changes were only required for the IA-64 ABI.


1/8/20   [EDGcpfe/22182]
IA-64 ABI demangling failure

Certain IA-64 mangled names (with multiple substitutions, involving templates)
could not be demangled properly.  One such example is
_Z1fIcEiN1XIXL_Z1CIT_EEEE4TypeEN1YIXL_ZS1_IS2_EEEE4TypeE.  That now demangles
to "int f<char>(X<C<T1>>::Type, Y<C<T1>>::Type)".


