Version 6.0, December 5, 2019

8/8/19   [EDGcpfe/21114]
Demangling certain local functions in the Cfront ABI

Some mangled names had failed to demangle properly when using the Cfront ABI.
Affected names have a local function indication immediately following
template arguments.  The following is a mangled name that had failed to
properly decode:

  for_each__tm__64_P17V__tm__9_XCiL_1_841__Ul1_FR17V__tm__9_XCiL_1_8__L1__exec__Fv__3stdFZ1ZT1Z2Z_Z2Z

It now decodes to:

  T2 std::for_each<T1, T2>(T1, T1, T2) [with T1=V<(int)8> *, T2=exec()::[lambda(V<(int)8> &) (instance 1)]]


07/25/19 [EDGcpfe/21614]
Increase MAX_ERRORS in mk_errinfo

The number of error messages in the front end has grown larger than the
3000 allocated.  That number has been increased to 10000.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 5.1, July 12, 2019

3/15/19  [EDGcpfe/20530,EDGcpfe/20644]
C++20: Demangling of char8_t

A change has been made to add demangling support for the C++20 char8_t type.
In the IA-64 ABI, "Du" is used to represent the type while "D8" is used in the
Cfront ABI.

Note that "Du" had previously been used (in the IA-64 ABI) to represent
__underlying_type and has been repurposed for char8_t.


1/8/19   [EDGcpfe/20702]
IA-64 ABI demangling of vector types

GCC 5.0 and later uses the string "Dv" to mangle vector types, and although
the IA-64 ABI document has not yet been updated to include this (as of this
writing), the "Dv" mangling is part of the <builtin-type> grammar production
which typically does not have a substitution recorded, except for vendor
extensions.  Since vector types were originally vendor extensions, it appears
that GCC makes an exception for these types as well.  The front end has always
recorded a substitution for vector types, but the decoding mechanism had
not previously expected one.  That has been changed and a mangled name like
_Z14_mm_packs_pi16Dv2_iS_ can now be properly demangled.


12/4/18  [EDGcpfe/20541]
IA-64 ABI demangling of vendor extended type qualifiers

The IA-64 ABI specifies a vendor extended type qualifier mangling:

  <extended-qualifier> ::= U <source-name> [<template-args>]
                                              # vendor extended type qualifier

Previously, only EDG-specific manglings were demangled, but a change has been
made to demangle non-EDG-specific uses of this mangling as well.


11/16/18 [EDGcpfe/20476]
Prelinker: Disable check for both instantiation and explicit specialization

The prelinker has the ability to check for the presence of both an
instantiation and an explicit specialization of an external entity.
This check can result in spurious errors in some cases.  Because it
can't be fixed without a mangling change, and only works in the cfront
ABI, it is now disabled by default.

Because of this issue, use of this feature is no longer recommended,
but it can be enabled by setting PL_DEFAULT_CHECK_SPECIALIZATION_ERRORS
to TRUE in edg_prelink.h, or by passing the "-s1" option to the prelinker.


