-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.13, February 22, 2017

10/18/16 [EDGcpfe/17433]
Demangling of nested template parameters in the Cfront ABI

Previously the invented names of template parameters used when demangling
Cfront mangled names had been re-used for some nested template cases, causing
demangled strings with the likes of "[with T1=T1]".  A change has been made to
use different template parameter names in such cases.  For example, the mangled
name f2__tm__2_i__FZ1Z_YOcl_2_18foo__tm__4_Z1Z__1NI1IO had been demangled as:

  decltype((N::foo<T1> [with T1=T1](param#1))) f2<T1>(T1) [with T1=int]

and is now:

  decltype((N::foo<U1> [with U1=T1](param#1))) f2<T1>(T1) [with T1=int]

There are no changes to mangled names.


