Version 4.11, May 12, 2016

5/10/16  [EDGcpfe/17165]
mk_errinfo: Add support for %d fill-in

The changes for EDGcpfe/16084 added the %d fill-in, but mk_errinfo had not
been updated to support it (with the -mml command-line option).  Now fixed.


2/26/16  [EDGcpfe/16845]
Remove __has_include and __has_include_next as predefined macros

A change has been made to make_predef_macro_table to eliminate __has_include
and __has_include_next as predefined macros that are copied from GNU
(these are implemented by the front end).


2/17/16  [EDGcpfe/16776]
Demangling of abi_tag attribute

A change has been made to be more consistent with the way GNU abi_tag
attributes are displayed in mangled names.  Tags are now annotated as
'[abi:tag]' rather than '__attribute((abi_tag("tag")))'.  The change
affects both IA-64 and Cfront ABIs.


2/11/16  [EDGcpfe/16687]
Demangling of co_await operator

A change has been made to demangle the co_await operator in both Cfront and
IA-64 ABIs.


1/18/16  [EDGcpfe/16757]
Cfront demangling of names starting with "__li"

As a result of demangling changes for demangling of user-defined literals
(EDGcpfe/9252), demangling of a Cfront name starting with "__li" had failed.
Now fixed.  The following example produces the mangled name "__lib__1NFv"
which had failed to be decoded:

  namespace N {
    void __lib();
  }
  int main() {
    N::__lib();
  }


12/20/15 [EDGcpfe/16731]
Demangling of local types in template argument lists

In the Cfront ABI, a local type that had appeared in a template argument list
had caused demangling to fail.  For this example (with --c++11):

  template <typename T> struct A {
    A() { while(0); }
  };
  void f() {
    struct LocalType {};
    A<LocalType> a;
  }

the mangled name __ct__32A__tm__23_20LocalType__L1__f__FvFv had failed to
be decoded and now decodes to:

A<T1>::A<f()::LocalType (instance 1)>() [with T1=f()::LocalType (instance 1)]


12/1/15  [EDGcpfe/16502]
--ms_extensions and --ms_compatibility command-line options

The eccp script has been updated to include the --[no_]ms_extensions and
--[no_]ms_compatibility command-line options.


7/25/15  [EDGcpfe/16011]
Clang compatibility: Predefined macros

The make_predef_macro_table utility has been modified to accept a new
--clang option.  The option takes a single argument: a pathname to a
clang executable which will be invoked to determine the list of predefined
macros that it defines (in both C and C++ modes).  The resulting
predefined_macros.txt file is suitable for use with clang emulation mode.

If using both GNU and clang emulation modes, make_predef_macro_table can
be invoked twice, once to generate GNU predefined macros and a second time
to generate clang predefined macros and the resulting files combined to create
a predefined_macros.txt file that will support both emulation modes.


6/26/15  [EDGcpfe/16348]
Add --c++17 command-line option to eccp

In preparation for the next version of the C++ standard, currently referred
to as C++17, the --c++17 command-line option has been added.  This option
currently has the same effect as --c++14.


6/24/15  [EDGcpfe/16339]
Demangling of qualified pointer-to-member constants

The demangled name of a pointer-to-member constant whose member is either
cv-qualified or ref-qualified (or both) had failed to include an indication of
either qualification.  This had been a problem in both the Cfront and IA-64
ABIs and is now fixed.  For example (with --c++11):

  struct A {
    void f() const &&;
  };
  typedef void (A::* PMF)() const &&;
  template<PMF P> struct B {
    B();
  };
  int main() {
    B<&A::f> b;
  }

Generates Cfront mangled name __ct__39B__tm__30_XCM1ACF_Ev_vLM0_L_2_n1_5f__1AFv
and IA-64 ABI mangled name _ZN1BIXadL_ZNKO1A1fEvEEEC1Ev which now demangle
to: "B<N1>::B<&A::f const&&>() [with N1=&A::f const&&]" and
"B<(&A::f const &&)>::B()" respectively.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.10.1, June 23, 2015

6/15/15  [EDGcpfe/16275]
IA-64 ABI: Incorrect demangled names for some pointer-to-member types

The IA-64 ABI typically records substitutions for cv-qualified and unqualified
versions of types that appear in a mangled name.  That rule does not apply
to function types where any ref- or cv-qualification is treated as an
indivisible part of the function type.  This had caused incorrect demangled
names for some types that involved pointer-to-member types and substitutions.
For example:

  struct A {};
  void f(void (A::*)() const, void (A::*)() const) {}

This results in a mangled name of: _Z1fM1AKFvvES1_.  The demangled name had
been:

  f(void (A::*)() const, void () const)

and is now:

  f(void (A::*)() const, void (A::*)() const)


6/12/15  [EDGcpfe/10878,EDGcpfe/16276]
Increase limit on length of demangled names

The edg_decode tool had limited the length of a demangled name to 15000 bytes;
that limit has been lifted (a dynamically-allocated buffer is now used and
reallocated in cases where the demangled name exceeds the original limit).


5/6/15   [EDGcpfe/16147]
Demangling of template argument packs

Mangled names that contained template argument packs had an extra set
of angle brackets in the demangled output.  In the example below
(with --c++11), the IA-64 ABI mangled name for f<A<int>> is
_Z1fIJ1AIJiEEEEvDpT_, but the demangled name had been
"void f<<A<<int>>>>(T1...)" and is now demangled to "void f<A<int>>(T1...)".
Similarly, the Cfront demangled name had been "void f<T1>(T1...) [with
T1...=<A<<int>>>]" and is now "void f<T1>(T1...) [with T1...=A<int>]".

  template<class... T> struct A {};
  template<class... Args> void f(Args... args);
  void g() {
    auto x = f<A<int>>;
  }


4/23/15  [EDGcpfe/15604,EDGcpfe/15397,EDGcpfe/15717,EDGcpfe/15851,
          EDGcpfe/16160]
Specifying target configuration at run time

The --target and --dump_legacy_as_target command-line options have been
added to the eccp script.  When the --target command-line option is given,
or if EDG_DEFAULT_TARGET is set, the directory searched for libraries,
typically $EDG_BASE/lib, is changed to include the configuration name, e.g.,
$EDG_BASE/lib_my_config if "--target my_config" is specified.  Also, the value
of the environment variable EDG_C_TO_OBJ_DEFAULT_OPTIONS_$target (where
$target is the name of the specified target configuration, e.g.,
EDG_C_TO_OBJ_DEFAULT_OPTIONS_my_config in this example) is used in place of the
EDG_C_TO_OBJ_DEFAULT_OPTIONS environment variable (to allow target-specific
options to be passed to the back end compiler, e.g., -m32).  See the Changes
entry in the src directory for more information.

In addition, front end command-line options that don't require a source file
(e.g., --version) no longer result in an error when eccp is invoked without
a source file.

A change has also been made to make_predef_macro_table to pass command-line
options other than --gcc and --g++ to gcc/g++.  This can be used to specify
options like -m32, for example.

A new tool, make_win_predef_macro_table.c, has been added that effectively
does what make_predef_macro_table currently does, but for Microsoft Visual
Studio rather than gcc.  That is, when compiled with a version of Microsoft
Visual Studio, it outputs the necessary predefined_macros.txt file to
generate the same predefined macros as Microsoft Visual Studio.  See
make_win_predef_macro_table.c for more information.


3/6/15   [EDGcpfe/16068]
eccp script hadn't allowed Clang C mode

Changes to the eccp script to allow Clang emulation mode inadvertently
neglected to allow Clang C emulation mode (i.e., --c --clang).  Now fixed.


1/28/15  [EDGcpfe/15939]
Demangling support for decltype(auto)

Demangling support for decltype(auto) has been added.  The IA-64 ABI uses the
string "Dc" to represent this type and the Cfront ABI uses the EDG-specific
"q" mangling.


1/27/15  [EDGcpfe/15897]
GNU compatibility: demangling for abi_tag attribute

Demangling support for the GNU "abi_tag" attribute has been added.  In the
IA-64 ABI case, the mangling follows that used by GNU (though not at present
part of the IA-64 ABI standard), namely using "B<count><tag>" as a suffix
to a name (where <count> indicates the number of characters in the <tag>
abi_tag attribute argument).  For the Cfront ABI, "__ab<count><tag>" is used
as a prefix to convey the same information.


