Version 4.8, October 18, 2013

8/28/13 [EDGcpfe/9167,EDGcpfe/12359]
C++11: Support for thread_local

Demangling of compiler-generated wrapper routine names that are introduced
in some front end configurations when lowering thread_local variables.
In the Cfront ABI, __THI__ and __THW__ are prefixed to the variable name
for the thread_local initialization and wrapper routines, respectively.

Also, edg_prelink has been updated to recognize the 'L' symbol type in
output from "nm" (for thread-local storage on Solaris systems).


7/19/13  [EDGcpfe/10662]
C++11 const-correctness

C++11 removed the previously-deprecated implicit conversion from a narrow
string literal to char*.  In order to permit their compilation as C++11
code, decode.c, edg_munch.c, edg_prelink.c, and mk_errinfo.c have been
changed to use the new a_const_char typedef that has been added to basics.h
(see the EDGcpfe/10662 entry in the src/Changes file for a more detailed
discussion), and mk_errinfo now uses that typedef in the output err_data.h
file.  In addition, dettarg.c has been changed to use const char instead of
char for pointers to read-only string data.


5/22/13  [EDGcpfe/14014]
Infinite loop caused stack overflow when demangling some IA-64 names

As a result of the demangling changes to handle the ambiguity that is
present in the IA-64 demangling for conversion functions (see the
Changes entry for EDGcpfe/10044), the demangling of certain conversion
function mangled names had resulted in an infinite loop during demangling
which caused a stack overflow.  For example, demangling "_ZN1AcvPT_IS1_EEv"
had caused this problem, now fixed.


