Version 4.5, October 5, 2012

9/4/12   [EDGcpfe/10617,EDGcpfe/11496,EDGcpfe/12018]
Add demangling for C++11 noexcept operator

Changes have been made to demangle the C++11 noexcept operator in both
IA-64 and Cfront ABIs.  The mangling string "nx" is used in both ABIs to
indicate a noexcept operator.  See the 9/3/12 Changes entry in the src
directory for more about the noexcept operator and specifier.


6/26/12  [EDGcpfe/9170]
Add demangling for C++11 brace-enclosed initializer lists

Changes have been made to demangle C++11 brace-enclosed initializer
lists in both IA-64 and Cfront ABIs.  The EDG-specific Cfront ABI mangling
mirrors that of the IA-64 ABI and uses the same character sequence
(i.e., "il" and "tl") for its encoding.  In the Cfront ABI, the "bi" sequence
is used to indicate a brace-enclosed initializer on a new/gcnew operation.


5/30/12  [EDGcpfe/12923]
Add demangling for g++ "restrict" qualifier in Cfront ABIs

The edg_decode tool has been updated to recognize the newly added
(and EDG-specific) "Dr" encoding for the "restrict" type qualifier in the
Cfront ABI (the IA-64 ABI already has an encoding for "restrict").


2/28/12  [EDGcpfe/11527]
Add --inline_statement_limit command line option to eccp

An --inline_statement_limit command line option has been added to eccp to
override the default limit on the maximum size of an inlined function.


2/21/12  [EDGcpfe/12717]
Handle label fill-in strings when producing error documentation

The mk_errinfo tool has been updated to handle the new label fill-in facility
by emitting the label value itself when producing documentation for
error codes (e.g., "the %[answer] is" is simply emitted as "the answer is"
in the documentation in the current font).


2/10/12  [EDGcpfe/11655]
Demangling of call operations where ADL is suppressed

Changes have been made to both IA-64 and Cfront ABI demangling to accommodate
the mangled named generated for a call operation where argument-dependent
lookup is suppressed by the use of parentheses.


1/22/12  [EDGcpfe/12622]
Add --c++03 command line option to eccp

A --c++03 command line option has been added to eccp to enable parsing of
C++ code that adheres to the ISO/IEC 14882:2003 standard.


