Version 4.4, December 21, 2011

12/13/11 [EDGcpfe/12513]
Remove __EXCEPTIONS from list of predefined macros

Change the make_predef_macro_table script so that it doesn't capture the
value of __EXCEPTIONS in the predefined-macros.txt file (by default this
macro is set by the front end as appropriate at run-time).


10/6/11 [EDGcpfe/12323]
Handle arguments with spaces in eccp

Previously, specifying an argument like -DCLASS="ref class" to eccp had
resulted in the argument being split into two separate arguments before being
passed to the front end, resulting in an error.  The script has been updated to
quote or escape arguments that contain spaces (as well as a set of other
characters which are interpreted by the shell).


9/14/11 [EDGcpfe/11746,EDGcpfe/11557]
Demangling of "this" in mangled names with late-specified return types

Changes have been made to both IA-64 and Cfront ABI demangling in order to
accommodate the mangled names generated by the front end when using "this" in
decltype expressions in late-specified return types in member functions, as
required by core issue 1207 (see N3282).  The IA-64 standard mangling ("fpT")
is now demangled in the IA-64 ABI case, and a parameter reference with a
parameter number of zero is treated as "this" in the Cfront case.


8/3/11  [EDGcpfe/8739,EDGcpfe/9831,EDGcpfe/9890,EDGcpfe/11024,EDGcpfe/11227]
GNU compatibility: 128-bit integer types

A change has been made to enable demangling of 128-bit integer types.  In the
Cfront-like ABI, these types have been assigned the encodings "m16" for
__int128_t and "Um16" for __uint128_t (following the types added for the
Microsoft __intN types -- see the Changes entry of 12/21/99).  The IA-64 ABI
standard encodings ("n" and "o") are used in the IA-64 configuration.


6/17/11 [EDGcpfe/8403,EDGcpfe/10669,EDGcpfe/11510,EDGcpfe/11628,EDGcpfe/11684,
         EDGcpfe/11800]
C++0x: Changes for char16_t/char32_t types

A change has been made to enable demangling of the new C++0x char16_t and
char32_t types.  In the Cfront-like ABI, these types have been assigned the
encodings "g" and "k", respectively.

The make_predef_macro_table script has been updated to suppress the
__CHAR16_TYPE__ and __CHAR32_TYPE__ macros from the predefined_macros.txt file.
These macros are now set by the front end.


4/8/11   [EDGcpfe/11620]
Add --c_to_obj_option option to eccp

A new option, --c_to_obj_option, has been added to the eccp script to
allow passing of command line options to the back end compiler.  The
command line argument that appears after --c_to_obj_option on the command
line is passed (without any interpretation) to the back end compiler.
For example:

  eccp --c_to_obj_option -Wall -x -c ex.c


