Version 4.3, March 17, 2011

3/15/11  [EDGcpfe/11177]
Variadic template name demangling

Changes have been made to both IA-64 and Cfront ABI demangling in
order to accommodate the mangled names generated by the front end when
processing variadic templates (a C++0x feature).  In the case of the IA-64 ABI,
we've submitted updates to the ABI spec and we conform to the updated
specification.  The front end documentation has been updated to include the new
mangling codes for the Cfront ABI.


1/7/11   [EDGcpfe/11254]
GNU C++ compatibility: __GXX_RTTI macro

The make_predef_macro_table script has been updated to suppress the __GXX_RTTI
macro from occurring in the predefined_macros.txt file.  This macro is now set
by the front end.


11/12/10 [EDGcpfe/11157]
Potential buffer overrun issue in mk_errinfo

An input buffer of exactly 32767 characters (not including the newline) had
resulted in a buffer overrun.  This has now been fixed (resulting in an
error message that the line is too long).


10/29/10 [EDGcpfe/11063]
Demangle encodings for C++/CLI handles and tracking references

The front end has introduced new mangled encodings for the C++/CLI concepts of
handles ("H" is used in the Cfront ABI and "U8__handle" in the IA-64 ABI) and
tracking references ("Tr" is used in the Cfront ABI and "U8__trkref" in the
IA-64 ABI).  A change has been made to demangle these mangled names.  Note that
the IA-64 ABI mangled encodings use a vendor extended type qualifier as
specified in the IA-64 ABI.  Using a vendor extension for type qualifiers to
represent these declarators avoids having to introduce an EDG-specific
modification to the IA-64 ABI (which may cause a conflict in future IA-64 ABI
revisions).


8/26/10  [EDGcpfe/10967]
Compilation error in decode.c when compiling lib_src on Mac OS X

A compilation error when scanning "using namespace std;" had occurred on
some platforms (e.g., Mac OS X) when compiling decode.c as part of lib_src.
This has now been fixed.


