Version 4.2, August 25, 2010

8/13/10  [EDGcpfe/10929]
Missing cv-qualification on certain demangled names (IA-64 ABI)

In cases where a substitution is used for a <template-prefix> and the
substitution has cv-qualifiers, those cv-qualifiers were not reflected in
the demangled name.  In this example, the two template functions have
distinct mangled names, but their demangled names had been the same:

  template <class T> struct A {};
  template <class T, class U> void f();
  void g() {
    f<A<char>, A<int> >();
    f<A<char>, const A<int> >();
  }


7/21/10  [EDGcpfe/10463]
Mangling changes to support new SFINAE rules

Substantial additions have been made to both IA-64 and Cfront ABI mangling in
order to accommodate the additional expression operators and constructs that
can arise because of the new SFINAE rules of WG21 paper N2634, and, in the
case of the IA-64 ABI, we've submitted updates to the ABI spec and we conform
to the updated specification.  The front end documentation has been updated to
include the new mangling codes for the Cfront ABI.


6/24/10  [EDGcpfe/10772]
Add --no_demangle option to eccp

A new option, --no_demangle, has been added to the eccp script to prevent
the post-processing of linker and nm output by the demangler (edg_decode).


3/24/10  [EDGcpfe/10148]
__cxa_demangle now available in the IA-64 ABI runtime library

Changes have been made to decode.c to allow decode.c to be cross
compiled (as part of the runtime library built in the lib_src directory).
Typically, decode.c is compiled for the host platform (and used as part of the
host-based edg_decode and edg_prelink tools).  The IA-64 ABI specifies that the
__cxa_demangle routine be available to programs on the target platform to
demangle mangled names.  decode.c can now be built for the target platform by
setting the new COMPILE_DECODE_FOR_LIB_SRC configuration macro to TRUE.  When
TRUE, header files from the front end are no longer included (although
header files from lib_src are now required).  Additionally, values for the
following configuration macros must be supplied: DEFAULT_EMULATE_GNU_ABI_BUGS
and USE_LONG_DOUBLE_FOR_HOST_FP_VALUE.  COMPILE_DECODE_FOR_LIB_SRC can only be
used with the IA-64 ABI (i.e., IA64_ABI must be TRUE).  Note that the
__cxa_demangle routine may be in the __cxxabiv1 namespace in certain runtime
configurations.


1/11/10  [EDGcpfe/10361]
Incorrect demangling of lambdas in static data member initializers (IA-64 ABI)

The demangled output for IA-64 ABI mangled names involving a lambda in a static
data member initializer was incorrect, causing substitutions that followed the
lambda to refer to incorrect entities.  In the example that follows, the
operator() for the lambda (whose mangled name is _ZNK1SI1AE1xMUlPS0_E_clES3_)
is now demangled properly ("S<A>::x::[lambda(A *) (instance 1)]::operator ()(A
*) const").

  struct A {};
  template <class T> struct S {
    static T *x;
  };
  template <class T> T *S<T>::x = [](T *s){ return s; }(nullptr);
  template A *S<A>::x;


1/9/10   [EDGcpfe/10044]
Incorrect demangling of IA-64 ABI template conversion operators

Mangled names of template conversion operators that contained substitutions
were incorrectly demangled.  This has now been fixed.  For example,
_ZN1ScvT_I1AIS2_IiEEEEv is now decoded as "S::operator T1<A<A<int>>>()".


1/7/10   [EDGcpfe/10132]
_Complex types not demangled properly in IA-64 ABI

_Complex types were not properly demangled when using the IA-64 ABI.  This has
now been fixed.  For example, _Z1fICdET_S1_ had failed to demangle and now
produces "T1 f<_Complex double>(T1)".


11/13/09 [EDGcpfe/10204]
Demangle IA-64 ABI builtin type vendor extensions

IA-64 builtin type vendor extensions that use the

  <builtin-type> ::= u <source-name>  # vendor extended type

rule are now properly demangled.  For example, _Z3foou11__va_list__ is now
decoded as foo(__va_list__).


10/14/09 [EDGcpfe/10142]
Buffer overflow when uncompressing invalid Cfront mangled name

When decode_identifier (when compiled to decode Cfront names) was given a
certain class of invalid mangled names (those indicating a compressed name,
where the name is longer than the indicated compressed length), the
output_buffer argument would be written to beyond size indicated by the
output_buffer_size argument.  The buffer overflow has now been fixed; an
error is indicated to the caller in *err (but *buffer_overflow_err is FALSE
because no amount of additional buffer space would allow the invalid input to
be properly uncompressed).  This invalid input would cause an overflow:
"__CPR5__12345Xoverflow".


10/1/09  [EDGcpfe/10129]
Offsets for demangled IA-64 thunk symbols show as large integers

The offsets of mangled names for IA-64 thunks were mistakenly displayed as
unsigned values, resulting in large positive values rather than negative
numbers.  This regression was introduced in 4.1 and is now fixed.  For example,
the mangled name _ZTv0_n24_N3c21D0Ev had produced (on 32 bit systems):

  Thunk for (offset 0, virtual offset 4294967272) c21::~c21() [deleting]

and now produces:

  Thunk for (offset 0, virtual offset -24) c21::~c21() [deleting]


9/30/09  [EDGcpfe/8623, EDGcpfe/9926, EDGcpfe/10102]
C++0x: Demangling support for nullptr

Support for demangling the new C++0x builtin type "decltype(nullptr)" has been
added.  The encodings for the new type are "Dn" (IA-64) and "n" (Cfront).
For example:

  template <class T> void f(T) {}
  void f1(void) {
    f(nullptr);   // IA-64:  _Z1fIDnEvT_
                  //         void f<std::nullptr_t>(T1)
                  // Cfront: f__tm__2_n__FZ1Z_v
                  //         void f<T1>(T1) [with T1=std::nullptr_t]
  }


9/14/09  [EDGcpfe/10090]
Prelinker: support for Mac OS Snow Leopard nm output

The prelinker has been updated to handle the nm output of Mac OS X 10.6
The "-fMacOSX64" option should be used on such systems.

See the edg_eccp_config.macosx file in the sample_edg_eccp_config
directory for more information about configuring eccp on Mac OS X.


8/20/09  [EDGcpfe/8232, EDGcpfe/9382]
Emit return type in IA-64 ABI decoding of template functions

The return type of mangled template functions is now emitted when demangling
IA-64 ABI mangled names (the return type was already emitted in the Cfront
ABI).  For example, the mangled name _Z1fIiEvf now produces the string
"void f<int>(float)".


