Version 3.8, July 14, 2006

No changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.7, January 12, 2006

10/10/05 mk_errinfo: incorrect test of STDLIB_H_INCLUDED

There was an incorrect test of STDLIB_H_INCLUDED in mk_errinfo.c.  This
could result in errors when compiling mk_errinfo.c in some environments.
Now fixed.

10/7/05  Prelinker: support for Mac OS X nm output

The prelinker has been updated to handle the nm output of Mac OS X 10.4.
The "-fMacOSX" option should be used on such systems.

See the edg_eccp_config.macosx file in the sample_edg_eccp_config
directory for more information about configuring eccp on Mac OS X.

10/2/05  Demangling for builtin operations

The demangler now demangles the new encodings for "builtin operations",
used to represent vendor-specific extensions.  Specifically, the
Microsoft __is_base_of operation is the first builtin operation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.6, June 7, 2005

5/11/05  eccp: path name of edg_decode program when using --nm option

The --nm option to eccp is a debugging feature used to run nm on the
object files created by a compilation.  The EDG_DECODE_PATH environment
variable, if set, is used by eccp to determine the pathname of the
edg_decode executable, but the --nm option did not make use of this
environment variable.  This has been fixed.

3/28/05  Minor prelinker cleanup

There were a few routines in edg_prelink.c that should have been declared
static, but were not.  In addition, pl_assertion_failed should have only
been included when CHECKING was enabled.  These are now fixed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.5, November 8, 2004

10/27/04 IA-64 name demangling: cv-qualifier on substitution

The IA-64 ABI demangler now correctly handles a cv-qualifier on a
substitution.

  _ZN1T1fEPKS_  --> T::f(const T*)
  _ZN1T1fEPKSa  --> T::f(const std::allocator*)

The "const" was missing on each of those previously.

10/13/04 eccp: one-instantiation-per-object and --cpfe_only option

If the --cpfe_only option was specified when using one-instantiation-per-object
mode, the .int.c files for the instantiation files were still being compiled
by the underlying C compiler, but should not have been.  This has been fixed.

7/9/04  Include guards added to getopt.h

On some systems, the system header files include getopt.h.  This can
result in getopt.h being included more than once when compiling the
prelinker.  Include guard code has been added to getopt.h to permit it
to be included more than once.

5/17/04 eccp: EDG_BASE directory exported

The EDG_BASE environment variable is now exported so that it can be used
by the front end to find the predefined macro file.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.4, May 8, 2004

4/14/04 Demangling of constructor name for class named __ctype

In general, user code is not allowed to use double underscores in
names, and demangling of such names cannot be guaranteed to work
in the Cfront-like ABI.  However, in the particular case in this
example, we were able to do a special-case workaround to allow a
class whose name begins with "__ct", for which the constructor name
__ct__7__ctypeFv was not correctly demangled previously.

  #define NAME __ctype
  class NAME {
  public:
      NAME(){};
  };
  int main(){
    NAME x;
  }

1/19/04 Demangling of vtable name with class beginning with "S"

Some virtual function table names were not demangled correctly in
the Cfront-like ABI.  Specifically, in a case like

  __vtbl__43MailPieceDirectionController__SharedTop2000__7Top2000

where a class name is used in a multi-level vtable name, and
the class name begins with a capital "S", the name mangler
failed to demangle the name.  ("__S" is the template
specialization indication, and fooled the demangler.)  Fixed.

8/16/03 Demangling of GNU min/max operators

The GNU min/max operators "<?" and ">?" were added in version 3.2, but
we forgot to update the demangler to handle them in mangled names.
That is now done, both for the IA-64 ABI:

  _ZN1Zv23maxERS_
  _ZN1Zv23minERS_
  _Z1gILi1EEv1AIXv23minT_Li2EEE
  _Z2g2ILi1EEv1AIXv23maxT_Li2EEE

and for the Cfront-like ABI:

  __mx__1ZFR1Z
  __mn__1ZFR1Z
  g__tm__9_XCiL_1_1__F26A__tm__17_XOmn2Z1ZCiL_1_2O_v
  g2__tm__9_XCiL_1_1__F26A__tm__17_XOmx2Z1ZCiL_1_2O_v

8/11/03 Demangling of virtual function table names, Cfront-like ABI

A change made in version 3.2 (see Changes entry of 7/10/03) broke
demangling of virtual function table names for classes whose names
begin with "Q".  Now working again.

  __vtbl__4Quid

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.3, July 31, 2003

7/18/03  Demangling for Microsoft explicit overriding extension

The name demangler (in both Cfront-like and IA-64 ABI modes)
has been enhanced to understand and demangle the encoding for
an explicitly overridden function for the Microsoft extension
that allows explicit specification of overriding.  See the
primary Changes file for details.

7/16/03  IA-64 ABI demangling, predefined substitutions as types

The IA-64 ABI demangler did not correctly demangle predefined
substitutions (e.g., "So") when they appeared as types; the
corresponding string was output twice.  The demangling was
correct when the predefined substitutions appear as members
of qualified names, which is usually where they appear.
Now fixed.  An example that gave incorrect output previously:

   _ZTVSo

7/15/03  Demangling fixes, Cfront-like ABI: not falling off end of items
         with lengths

The name mangling scheme for the Cfront-like ABI uses lengths preceding
certain items.  In some cases, the demangler did not properly stop
scanning a subitem at the end of the number of characters indicated
in the length, and because of that failed to demangle a name
properly.  This happened in particular when a type or list of types
appeared at the end of the subitem.  Now fixed.

   __nw__18X__L0__main__FiPPcSFUi

This involved a fairly large set of changes to decode.c, though for
the most part they are mechanical.  The demangling for the IA-64 ABI
was not affected (it does not use lengths).

7/10/03  Demangling fixes, Cfront-like ABI: virtual function table names,
         function-local entities

Several demangling problems have been fixed in the Cfront-like ABI:

-- A virtual function table name in which a base class name has more
   than one derivation step is now demangled correctly

   __vtbl__38B__L0__main__FiPPc__D__L1__main__FiPPc__18F__L2__main__FiPPc

   (The fix for the Changes entry of 2/19/03 was not quite right.)

-- A virtual function name in a pointer-to-member constant is now
   demangled correctly when it is a member of a local class

   g__FP53X__tm__44_XCMQ2_1A1BFQ2_1A1B_vLM0_L_2_n1_10f__Q2_1A1B

-- Certain address-of-member references are now demangled correctly

   f__tm__8_X5v__1B__FR13A__tm__5_XZ1Z_v

-- Certain function-local types are now fully identified in the
   demangled name.  Formerly, they did not give the containing
   function information.

   __ct__15A__L0__main__FvFv

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.2, May 12, 2003

5/6/03   Demangling for __alignof__ operator, IA-64 ABI

The mangling code for the __alignof__ operator in the IA-64 ABI
has been changed to make it match the one used by g++.  The 
demangler has been updated accordingly.

4/15/03  Prelinker: memory allocation error

When using one-instantiation-per-object mode, the prelinker allocated
one too few bytes of memory when constructing the instantiation file
name.  This has been fixed.

3/19/03  Compilation of mk_errinfo.c on MacOS X 10.2.x

MacOS X 10.2.x places malloc.h in a "sys" subdirectory.  mk_errinfo.c was
updated to compile correctly on that platform.

2/20/03  Demangling of non-nested type names with template arguments,
         Cfront-like ABI

In version 3.1, the Cfront-like ABI mangling for a type that is
not nested but does have template arguments changed to include
leading underscores and a length.

Old: MyTemp__tm__2_i
New: __15MyTemp__tm__2_i

These names are not external, and as such the demangler is not
strictly speaking required to handle them.  However, it did handle
the old form, so it has been updated to also handle the new form.

2/19/03  Demangling of virtual function table names, Cfront-like ABI

Certain mangled names of virtual function tables in the Cfront-like
ABI did not demangle correctly.  Now fixed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.1, January 26, 2003

1/2/03   Prelinker: diagnose attempt to build without automatic instantiation

The prelinker requires that AUTOMATIC_TEMPLATE_INSTANTIATION be TRUE in
order to build properly.  A preprocessor check and #error directive have
been added to enforce this requirement.

12/05/02 eccp: .ii/.ti file options when not using automatic instantiation

In some cases the eccp script would pass the --ii_file and/or
--template_info_file options to the front end even when automatic
instantiation was disabled in eccp.  This has been fixed.

11/26/02 Prelinker: support for IA-64 alternate entry points

A new .ti file entry kind has been added to handle alternate entry
points for constructors and destructors when using the IA-64 ABI in
conjunction with INSTANTIATE_EXTERN_INLINE.  The prelinker has been
updated to process the new entries.

10/8/02  eccp: allow .s files to be used

Assembler files with a .s suffix may now be included on the eccp command
line.  Such files are compiled by the underlying C compiler.

9/12/02  Demangling fixes: closing delimiters on sizeof(expr) and []

The demangling for expressions in the Cfront-like ABI got closing
delimiters wrong in two cases:  "sizeof(expr)" came out as "sizeof(expr"
(missing closing parenthesis), and "x[y]" came out as "x[]y".  (At the
moment, it's not thought to be possible to get the front end to put
put a [] operator in a mangled name, but it probably will be in
the future.)

9/11/02  Demangling for IA-64 ABI

The demangler now understands the name mangling of the IA-64 ABI
when IA64_ABI is set to TRUE.

7/9/02   eccp: eliminated use of "match" option

eccp made use of the "match" option of the expr command.  This option is
not supported on some versions of expr (notably newer verions of Solaris).
The ":" form of the option, which is more widely available, is now used
instead.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.0, May 9, 2002

5/8/02   Demangling of names with nested externalized function names

Names of variables promoted out of externalized static functions
are now demangled correctly.  An example of a name that formerly
was not demangled is

x__L4____STF__sft3__tm__9_1Z2AA2AA__FZ1ZRCZ2__tm__2_sZRCZ3__tm__2_sZ_RC1Z__test_7_c_e9076052

4/17/02  Demangling of nested unnamed namespaces

The special mangling for a nested unnamed namespace, __N with nothing
following it, is now demangled correctly as <unnamed>.

4/17/02  Demangling of local class names

A bug in the demangling of local class names has been fixed.
An example of a mangled name that was not demangled correctly
is __STF____dt__10LC2__L6097Fv__test_1_c_garr1.

4/3/02   Demangling of sizeof(expression)

A new encoding for a sizeof operator applied to an expression is
now generated by the front end and demangled by the demangler.
The "sz" for sizeof is followed by "e" to indicate an expression
instead of a type.  Also applies to alignof and uuidof.

3/2/02   Prelinker: invalid .ti file changed to normal error

If the contents of the .ti file become corrupted, the prelinker would
issue an internal error.  A common cause of a corrupted .ti file is the
fact that the file as written by the front end is invalid until it is
later updated by the driver (because the command-line information is missing
from the file written by the front end).  The internal errors have been
replaced with an error that indicates that the template information file
is corrupted.

2/14/02  Demangling of template member addresses in nontype template arguments

A bug in demangling for nontype template arguments that are the address
of a member that is a template instance has been corrected.  An example
of a name that was not demangled correctly is

__dt__73CT7__tm__62_XCPFSc_Sc50mt1__tm__3_Sc__Q2_2N127CT6__tm__16_XCPFSc_Sc3tf11BFv

1/18/02  Demangling of virtual function table names for ambiguous base classes

The name mangling for virtual function tables for ambiguous base classes
has been changed in some cases: the "__A" suffix now sometimes has a
number following it to distinguish multiple ambiguous base classes with
the same name.  The demangler has been changed to demangle such names.

8/9/01   eccp: exit status for generated C compilation errors

If the underlying C compiler exits with a non-zero status, eccp now
returns an abort status to distinguish this case from a case where
the front end reports errors.

8/2/01   Prelinker: removal of one-instantiation-per-object files

The prelinker removes object files created in one-instantiation-per-object
mode when it detects the files are no longer needed.  If an explicit
instantiation of a template was added to some other file, the prelinker
could mistakenly remove the object created by the compilation of the
other file.  This could result in a prelinker loop or other incorrect
behavior.  This has been fixed.

7/19/01  Prelinker: handling of internal errors

The prelinker now uses the front end configuration flag EXIT_ON_INTERNAL_ERROR
to specify how the prelinker should exit when an internal error is detected.
The prelinker now calls abort() if EXIT_ON_INTERNAL_ERROR is FALSE.

6/27/01  Prelinker: detection of instantiation loops

An error in the data structures passed to the prelinker, or an inconsistency
between the data structures and the generated object code can result in
a prelinker loop in which the same entity is repeatedly assigned to and
removed from a given file.  The prelinker now detects such cases and
issues an internal error.  Because this will detect the most common cases
of instantiation loops, the limit on the number of prelinker iterations has
been increased to 300 to permit the use of more deeply recursive templates.

1/15/01  eccp: Temporary file not removed in some cases

When using one instantiation per object mode, a temporary file used by
eccp (named "il<process-id>") did not get removed when using the -k or
--keep_gen_c option.  This has been fixed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.45, December 26, 2000

12/13/00 Demangling of "?" operator in template names

The name demangler now correctly handles the "?" operator in
expressions in nontype template arguments.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.44, August 1, 2000

3/22/00  eccp: environment variable changes

The eccp environment variable EDG_DEFAULT_LIB_PATHS, which specifies
the library paths implicitly used by the linker, has been renamed
EDG_LINKER_LIB_PATHS.  EDG_DEFAULT_LIB_PATHS is now used for a new
variable that provides a list of library path directives that is
passed to both the prelinker and linker.

12/21/99 Mangling for Microsoft __intN types

The name demangler can now demangle the encoding for the Microsoft-specific
integer types __int8, __int16, __int32 and __int64 (and their unsigned
variants).  These are distinct built-in types when emulating Microsoft Visual
C++ 6.0 and higher (earlier versions treat these types as typedefs for standard
integer types).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.43, December 8, 1999

12/1/99  Mangling for template template parameters

The name demangler can now demangle template template parameters.

12/1/99  Demangling of unnamed namespace names

The mangled form of an unnamed namespace name now includes a unique
string after the "__N".  The demangler has been updated to ignore the
extra characters, and put out "<unnamed>".

8/17/99  Utility program build problems in strict C++ mode

The utility programs have been updated so that they compile properly
in strict C++ mode.  Some of the problems were a result of the change to
make string literals const.  Others were related to the linkage of the
function pointer passed to the qsort and bsearch routines.

8/13/99  Prelinker: build problem on some systems

The prelinker did not compile on some systems (e.g., Red Hat 6.0) on which
the assignment of stderr to a FILE* is not a static initialization.  Now fixed.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.42, August 12, 1999

8/11/99  Demangling of promoted local static names

Certain mangled names of promoted local static variables were not
demangled correctly (e.g., i__L14__f__Fv).  Now fixed.

8/4/99   Prelinker: Default SGI nm options changed for Irix 6.x

The options passed to the nm command on Irix have been changed from
"-Bopg" to "-Bop", which we are told is the appropriate set of options
for Irix 6.x.

7/28/99  Prelinker: informational messages now directed to stderr

Formerly, information messages (e.g., "f(int) assigned to t.c") were
directed to standard output.  They are now directed to the standard
error device instead.

7/2/99   Prelinker: error output of "nm" command no longer discarded

Formerly, any error output of the "nm" command was discarded.  It
will now go to wherever stderr is directed.

6/23/99  Demangling of invalid name like x__1

An invalid name like x__1 was demangled as ::x.  Now, an error is
reported.

6/2/99   Instantiation object suffix when not using the C-generating back end

The prelinker removes instantiation object files that are no longer needed.
To do so, it must know the file suffix that is used for such files.
Formerly, it assumed that the suffix was either ".int.o" or ".int.obj",
neither of which is correct when a "real" back end is being used.  The
prelinker now uses ".o" or ".obj" when the back end is not the C or C++
generating back end.

4/27/99  Prelinker accepts nm code of "R" for read-only variable definition

The Linux "nm" command uses a type code of "R" to indicate the definition
of a variable that can be placed in read-only memory.  The prelinker
has been modified to recognize this type code.

4/27/99  Prelinker calls fopen with a null file name

A bug in edg_prelink caused it to call fopen with a null file name pointer.
This happens to work on most systems, but is not correct.  Now fixed.

4/17/99  Incorrect required_buffer_size returned on attempt to demangle
         compressed name

The demangler returns a required_buffer_size, intended to allow the caller
to allocate a larger buffer for the output if the demangled form of the
name will not fit in the buffer.  When the input mangled name is a
compressed name, the value returned was not large enough (the routine
uses the buffer also as working storage to uncompress the name, and
the size passed back to the caller did not account for that space
requirement).  As a consequence, the demangling process would fail
even when a buffer of the requested size was provided.  Now fixed.

Note that if the buffer size given is smaller than the size of the
uncompressed mangled name, the size returned will be enough to uncompress
the name but not enough to produce the demangled form.  The caller must
be prepared in that case to loop a second time (the length returned
the second time will be correct).  [Patch sent out 5/27/99.]

3/16/99  Demangling of compressed names

In some cases, the demangler failed to demangle compressed mangled names.
Now fixed.  [Patch sent out 3/19/99.]

3/12/99  Prelinker problem in copy-if-nonlocal mode

When the processing for template information files was added a bug was
introduced in copy-if-nonlocal mode that would cause the remote instantiation
request file to be updated instead of the local one when a remote instantiation
request file was copied to the local directory.  This has been fixed.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.41, March 5, 1999

2/17/99  Compression in mangled names

The name demangler now uncompresses mangled names, which begin with "__CPR".

2/16/99  "uu" for __uuidof operator in mangled encoding of expression

The encoding "uu" is now used for the Microsoft __uuidof operator
in the mangled encoding for an expression.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.40, December 8, 1998

No changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.39, August 10, 1998

7/30/98  Prelinker fails when object file name is also an archive member name

A bug was introduced into the prelinker in version 2.37, when
one-instantiation-per-object support was added, that would cause the
prelinker to fail if an object file name specified on the command-line
was the same as an object file name found in an archive that is being
used.  This has been fixed.

7/29/98  eccp: driver name can be changed for diagnostic purposes

The eccp script now uses a variable for the driver name to be displayed
in diagnostic messages, making it simpler for those who would like to
use a different name for the script.

7/29/98  Ignore "--" option in eccp

The eccp script now ignores the "--" option.

7/29/98  Handling of duplicate names in edg_munch

The "nm" command on some systems produces duplicate entries for __sti
and __std functions, causing edg_munch to call the routines more than
once.  edg_munch has been modified to detect duplicate entries, but
only if they are adjacent to one another in the "nm" output.

7/10/98  Prelinker erroneously finds .ti file for archive

The prelinker used information from a template information (.ti) file
even when the associated file was a library (.a or .lib) file.  Template
information files should only be used when the associated file is an
object (.o or .obj) file.  This has been fixed.

7/10/98  Return type of __sti routines

Originally, the return type of the __sti routines generated by the
front end was "char".  In version 2.18 this was changed to "void", but
edg_munch was not changed accordingly.  edg_munch has now been changed
to match the front end.

6/3/98   Prelinker does not handle nonlocal files properly in
         one-instantiation-per-object mode

When using one-instantiation-per-object mode, the prelinker does not handle
nonlocal instantiation files properly.  When files are linked using
a command such as

	eccp --one some_dir/a.o b.o

"some_dir" needs to be used as a prefix to the instantiation directory
specified in some_dir/a.ti.  This has been fixed.

5/31/98  INSTANTIATION_OBJECT_SUFFIX set incorrectly when __MICROSOFT_OS__
         is TRUE

edg_prelink.h did not set INSTANTIATION_OBJECT_SUFFIX properly when
__MICROSOFT_OS__ is TRUE.  This would cause the prelinker to fail when
one-instantiation-per-object mode was used on such systems.

4/27/98  Prelinker problem when nonlocal files are used in conjunction with
         a definition list file

When a definition list file is being used and nonlocal files are specified,
a local and nonlocal file could both end up "adopting" the same instantiation,
resulting in a prelinker internal error.  This has been fixed.

4/25/98  Demangling of virtual function table names with three parts

The name demangler now demangles virtual function tables that name three
classes, as in "virtual function table for A in B in C".  Such names are
used for virtual function tables generated for use during subobject
destruction or construction in the presence of virtual base classes.

3/25/98  Output file option must be included in the instantiation command line
         in eccp

The eccp script did not include the -o option in the instantiation command
line.  This would cause the prelinker to fail after recompiling a file that
was originally compiled with the -o option.  This has been fixed.

3/3/98   Template information files not handled correctly by -o option in eccp

When using the -o option to specify an object file name for a compilation
(i.e., when the -c option is also being used) eccp did not pass the
--template_info_file option to the front end to indicate the name of
the template information file to be created.  This has been fixed.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.38, January 13, 1998

1/11/98  Demangling of some ambiguous mangled names

Some mangled names using an old form for literal lengths (the cfront
form) that causes some ambiguities were not successfully demangled by
edg_decode, and cfront's demangler manages to handle them.  Those cases
are now demangled by edg_decode as well.  Examples:

  f01__FPF15S__pt__7_XCiL15_v
  f03__FM1CF15S__pt__7_XCiL15_v

12/18/97 Prelinker gets internal error when file name contains a drive
         specification

On Windows 95 or Windows NT, the prelinker would get an internal error
if an object file name or library name included a drive specification.
This has been fixed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.37, October 18, 1997

11/25/97 Prelinker problem when not using .ti files

The prelinker could abort or create an invalid .ii file when configured
to not use a .ti file and when a .ii file was removed.  This has been
fixed.

10/16/97 --list_object_files option to eccp (-b option to prelinker)

An option has been added to the eccp script and prelinker to permit
a list of object files to be displayed.  This is intended to be
used with the --one_instantiation_per_object option to get a list
of object files that includes the generated instantiation object files.
This option can be used when generating a library, for example:

  ar r mylib.a `eccp --one_instantiation_per_object --list_object_files *.o`

10/15/97 Improved interface between the prelinker and front end

The interface between the front end and prelinker has been modified to
reduce the number of times that the front end must be invoked to
generate the complete set of instantiations needed by a program.
See the front end Changes file entry for more information.

10/15/97 Improved diagnostic when instantiation is assigned to more than
         one .ii file

If the prelinker detects that an instantiation has been assigned to
more than one .ii file, the names of the first two files in which the
instantiation was found are now displayed.  This situation can occur
if an overlapping set of object files is used to link two different
programs.

10/13/97 Ability to put instantiation flags in a separate file

The prelinker and eccp script have been modified to make use of
template information files generated by the front end.  See the front
end Changes file entry for more information.

10/9/97  Name demangling: __STF__ form for externalized static functions

Static functions made external (for the one-instantiation-per-object-file
feature) are now mangled with names beginning with __STF__.  The name
demangler now decodes that form.

10/8/97  Abbreviated command line options

The eccp script now accepts abbreviated keyword command line options.
Only as many initial characters as are required to uniquely identify
an option are needed.  For example, "--bo" may be used to specify
the "--bool" option.

9/28/97  Name demangling: __STV__ form for externalized statics

Static variables made external are now mangled with names beginning
with __STV__.  The name demangler now decodes that form.

7/24/97  EDG_INCLDIR environment variable used by eccp

The eccp script now uses EDG_INCLDIR, if set, as the default include directory
when compiling C++ code (EDG_CINCLDIR was already used as the default
directory when compiling C).  If this environment variable is not set,
EDG_BASE/include is used.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.36, June 17, 1997

4/22/97  Building the prelinker on Windows

edg_prelink.c was including unistd.h, which is not necessarily available
under Windows.  Also, on Windows the popen() and pclose() functions must
be called using the names _popen() and _pclose(). 

4/11/97  Name demangling: cfront-style local names

decode.c now recognizes and demangles cfront-style local names, e.g.,
"__2i" for "i".

4/11/97  Name demangling: function-local names

decode.c now understands more mangled names of entities local to
functions.  The name of the function is also now put out at the beginning
of the name, followed by "::", which works better for multi-level names.

  func__15A__L0__main__FvFv  --> main()::A::func()
  i__L0__f__tm__2_i__FZ1Z_v  --> void f<T1>(T1) [with T1=int]::i

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.35, February 28, 1997

2/24/97  Name demangling: index in pointer-to-member-function

decode.c did not understand a length on the index field of a pointer-to-
member-function encoding when the length used the new form ("_nnn_").
Now fixed.

2/7/97   Memory allocation error in prelinker

Under certain circumstances the prelinker would not allocate sufficient
memory for the construction of the command line used to recompile a
file.  This has been fixed.

1/3/97   Invariant name used in "removed" error codes

The enumeration name used for "removed" error messages has been changed
to use the error message number instead of a counter of removed messages.
This was done to eliminate gratuitous changes in the error codes from
one release to another.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.34, December 18, 1996

12/13/96 Name demangling for partial specializations

The name demangler now recognizes the "__ps__" marker that introduces
the first template argument list on a partial specialization of a
class template.

12/11/96 Speed improvement on name demangling

The name demangling code was agonizingly slow on demangling very large
names (a 3000-character name could take 10 minutes on a workstation).
The offending piece of the algorithm has been changed.

11/4/96  Demangling of names for interface routines for covariant return types

The implementation of virtual functions with covariant return types
uses interface routines with names that begin with "__VFE__".  These
are now demangled correctly.

10/22/96 decode.h and decode.c copyrighted but not proprietary

We've changed the copyright notices in decode.h and decode.c to make
those files freely redistributable.  They're copyrighted, but they're
not proprietary.  This was done to allow incorporation of those files
into the GNU debugger gdb, and debuggers in general.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.33, October 2, 1996

9/26/96  Name demangler and initialization guard variables for local statics

Local static variables of extern inline functions are now promoted out
of the functions and made external so that all copies of the function
will use the same static variables.  The initialization guard variables
for those local statics are also made external, and they have mangled
names beginning with "__LSG__", followed by the mangled name for the
promoted local variable.  The name demangler now demangles such guard
variable names.

9/26/96  Name demangler and names of types/variables promoted out of functions

The name demangler can now demangle names of variables and types promoted
out of functions in IL lowering.  The "__Lnn" piece of such mangled names
has been moved to between the local entity name and the mangled name of
the function, instead of at the end, to make demangling easier.  The scope
number in the "__Lnn" has also been made relative to the function.
(These two changes have no ABI implications, since such names have been,
by definition, internal to a compilation.)  A mangled name like
"j__L2__f__Fv" (formerly something like "j__f__Fv__L10") is now demangled
as "j in block 2 of function f()".

9/24/96  -b option failed to restore C++ mode in eccp

The -b option (cfront compatibility) should cause eccp to operate
in C++ mode.  A bug prevented this from occurring.  This has been
fixed.

9/24/96  mk_errinfo can now generate MML documentation files

The -mml option has been added to mk_errinfo.  This option causes it
to produce a file in MML format.  MML is "Maker Markup Language", a
language that can be imported into FrameMaker.

9/17/96  --strip option added to eccp

The --strip option has been added to the eccp script.  This option causes
the "strip" command to be run on the executable file that is produced.

8/13/96  "K" for extern C recognized by name demangler

The name demangler now recognizes a "K" following the "F" for a function
type as indicating an function type with extern "C" linkage.  The "K"
is just ignored; there's no representation for this information in
the demangled form.

7/23/96  Added option to eccp to convert relative -I paths to absolute paths

An option has been added to the eccp script that causes it to convert
relative include directory paths to absolute paths when building the
command line in the .ii file.  This is sometimes necessary when using
the --prelink_copy_if_nonlocal option.  In such cases, path names that
are relative to the original directory need to be converted into
absolute path names in order for the command line to be correct
when copied to the new directory.  This option is enabled by
setting the environment variable EDG_USE_ABSOLUTE_INCL_DIR_PATHS to 1.

7/2/96   Incorrect error test in mk_errinfo

mk_errinfo was incorrectly checking for an error when opening the err_data.h
file.  This could result in an abort if the file could not be opened.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.32, June 28, 1996

5/25/96  Prelinker diagnostic when nm exits with an error

The prelinker now issues a warning if the nm command that is
executed returns a nonzero return status.

5/15/96  Improved prelinker message when .ii file is not writable

A better diagnostic is now issued if the .ii file is not writable
when the prelinker attempts to update it.  The diagnostic now
indicates the file name and the fact that it is not writable.

5/6/96   Name demangler enhancements for distinct template mangling

The name demangler has been enhanced to deal with the new form of
mangling for templates.  See the primary Changes file for details
on the new encodings.

5/6/96   Error if an entity is both specialized and instantiated

The prelinker now issues an error if an entity is referenced as both
an explicit specialization and a generated instantiation.  This
feature will only work if the special name mangling for specializations
is enabled in the front end.  The feature can be enabled or disabled
using the -s1 or -s0 option to the prelinker.  The default value for
this option is specified by the PL_DEFAULT_CHECK_SPECIALIZATION_ERRORS
flag in edg_prelink.h.

3/4/96   Error status returned by prelinker when recompiles fail

The prelinker uses the system() function to recompile source files
to generate instantiations.  When the eccp command returns a nonzero
status (via the system() function) to the prelinker, the system()
function shifts the return status 8 bits to the left before
returning it.  The prelinker has been modified to adjust the
return value by shifting it back to the right.

2/28/96  Configuration file that defines variables used by eccp

eccp now looks in the directory specified by the EDG_BASE environment
variable for a file named edg_eccp_config.  If such a file exists,
eccp includes it to define additional environment variables that may
be needed.

2/22/96  Bug in name demangling of nested class name in virtual function
         table name

In version 2.30 of the front end, name mangling for virtual function tables
was changed to make it match cfront more closely.  The change duplicated
a quirk of the cfront name mangling scheme, one that doesn't really make
much sense.  Specifically, the virtual function table for the class A::B
is now put out as __vtbl__7Q2_1A1B; note the length "7" in front of the
nested class name, which was not present before version 2.30.  This change
unfortunately confused the name demangler, which is understandable since
the name is ambiguous: the new form is also the name that is generated if
the programmer has a class called "Q2_1A1B".  The demangler has now been
changed to recognize this case and treat it as the nested class name
instead of the less-likely "Q2_1A1B".

2/22/96  Reentrancy in name demangler

The state variables used in decode.c have been moved into a structure, and
a pointer to the structure is passed around.  This allows the name demangler
to be used where reentrancy is required.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.31, January 19, 1996

1/17/96  eccp option to prelink object files to be put in a library

The --prelink_objects option has been added to eccp.  This option
causes object files to be processed by the prelinker, but suppresses
the actual link step.  This can be used to prelink a set of object
files that are to be put into a library.

1/17/96  eccp and prelinker option to remove instantiation flags

The --remove_instantiation_flags option has been added to eccp.  This
option causes the prelinker to recompile all of the source files
associated with the object files being linked using the
--suppress_instantiation_flags option, which suppresses
the generation of the __TIR__, __CBI__, and __DNI__ flags in
the generated object files.

1/10/96  edg_prelink inserts escapes before quotes in command line

The prelinker now inserts an escape before quotes found in the
compilation command line in the .ii file.

1/4/96   Permit verbose mode to be turned off in the prelinker

A new configuration flag has been added to edg_prelink.h called
PL_DEFAULT_VERBOSE_MODE.  This lets you specify whether or not
the prelinker should produce verbose output by default.  A new
command line option (-q) has been added to the prelinker that specifies
that verbose output should not be produced. 

12/27/95 Building the utility programs with the Sun C++ compiler

The changes have been made that are necessary for the utility programs
to be compiled  with the Sun C++ compiler on SunOS 4.1.3.

12/22/95 Use of malloc.h in edg_prelink.c and edg_munch.c

These files no longer include malloc.h when __ANSIC__ is defined.

10/12/95 edg_munch option to ignore initial input lines

edg_munch now support a command line option that causes it to ignore
the initial N lines of input.  This is useful on systems like
Solaris that include a header in the nm output.  The option 
is -iN, where N is the number of lines to be ignored.

10/12/95 Change in path used for nm on Solaris in edg_prelink

edg_prelink now looks for nm in the user's search path on Solaris
instead of having a directory name included in the default nm command.

10/12/95 New eccp environment variable for edg_munch options

The environment variable EDG_MUNCH_OPTIONS can now be used to
specify the options to be passed to edg_munch.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.30, October 10, 1995

10/10/95 mk_errinfo updated to handle %np error message fill-ins

The mk_errinfo program now supports the %np fill-in used to
force the parameter types to appear when function name appears
in a symbol fill-in.

9/20/95  eccp support for naming object files

The -o option may now be used in conjunction with the -c option
to name the object file generated by a compilation.  This feature
uses the new --ii_file command line option of the front end to
ensure that the .ii file name matches the name of the object file
being generated.

8/21/95  Missing newline at end of file given to edg_decode

If final line of the input to edg_decode ends without a newline, and a
mangled identifier is the last thing on that line, a garbage character
(== EOF) was written to the output file.  Now fixed.

8/21/95  Display of false and true in name demangling

Name demangling now puts out false and true in template arguments of
bool type (formerly, (bool)0 and (bool)1 were put out).

7/26/95  Checking return value of popen in edg_prelink

edg_prelink did not check the return value of popen to determine
whether an error occurred.  This could result in an abort if
the nm process could not be created for some reason.  This has
been fixed.

7/26/95  Executable permissions when using "patch" with eccp

eccp has been changed to respect the umask setting when changing
the permissions on the executable file when using "patch" to
handle static initialization.

7/21/95  eccp and prelinker support for -Bstatic and -Bdynamic

The -Bstatic and -Bdynamic options are now supported by eccp and
edg_prelink.  This support consists of passing the options along to the
linker retaining their position relative to the object files and
libraries specified on the command line.

7/21/95  eccp and the -G option

eccp now supports the -G option for building shared libraries.  This
option is passed to the linker and causes eccp to suppress the
patch/munch phase when created the linked output file.

7/21/95  eccp and reporting prelinker failures

Formerly, a prelinker failure (returning a nonzero status) would not
by itself cause eccp to return a failure status (the assumption was
that a prelinker error would also result in a linker error).  Now,
to be sure that an error will not go unnoticed, eccp will always return
an failure status if the prelinker fails.

5/30/95  eccp bug using expr command

The eccp script contained two expr commands that were not properly formed.
These caused problems on some systems (e.g., Linux).

5/25/95  Prelinker diagnostic issued if nm produces no output

The prelinker now issues a warning when nm produces no output.
This is usually an indication that there is some sort of
configuration problem (e.g., looking for the nm command in the
wrong place).

5/25/95  Prelinker bug handling first line of an archive

A bug in edg_prelink resulted in the first line of nm output for an
archive file to be ignored.  This has been corrected.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.29, May 24, 1995

5/3/95   Mangled codes for array new (nwa) and array delete (dla) are
	 now demangled

5/2/95   Mangled code "b" is demangled as "bool"

3/28/95  eccp and the order of object files and libraries passed to the linker

Formerly, eccp maintained separate lists of object files, libraries
specified as full path names, and libraries specified using the
-lname option.  These lists were then passed separately to the linker.
Now, a single list is maintained preserving the order specified by the
user.  This change required a corresponding change in the prelinker.

3/22/95  Header files used by mk_errinfo

Uses of nonstandard header files have been removed from mk_errinfo.c.

3/18/95  Demangling of local variable names

Variable names of the form "__nn_mm_name", where "nn" and "mm" are decimal
numbers, are generated by the C-generating back end for local variables.
These are now decoded by decode.c.  This is not intended to be a complete
solution to demangling local names; this just happens to be one easy
case that's frequently asked for.

3/3/95   eccp use of --gen_c_file_name option 

When compiling multiple source files, eccp would keep appending additional
--gen_c_file_name options to the string passed to the front end.  This
worked, as the front end would use the last name passed (which was the
right one).  Only the correct name is passed now.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.28, March 2, 1995

1/13/95  Allow multi-character symbol types in HP/UX nm output

Some versions of HP/UX nm produce multi-character types such as "TS".
edg_prelink now allows (and discards) additional characters in the
type field when the -fHPUX option is used.

1/11/95  Mangled code "w" is demangled as "wchar_t"

1/3/95   Incorrect handling of HP/UX nm output

A bug has been fixed in edg_prelink that caused the prelinker to
incorrectly process the nm output under HP/UX.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.27, December 22, 1994

12/20/94 Change in -p option

The -p option is now used to indicate that profiling code is
to be generated.  This option is passed to the underlying
C compiler and causes _p to be appended to library names specified
by the -l option.

Formerly, this option indicated that the file should be compiled in
C++ mode.  This may now be specified using the --c++ option.

12/20/94 EDG_LIBRARY_OPTION

The EDG_LIBRARY_OPTION may be used to specify the string used as the
library directory option name.  The default value is -L.

12/20/94 Change in EDG_STD_LIBS

Formerly, EDG_STD_LIBS contained a string to be passed to the linker
such as "-lstd -lxyz".  It has been changed to a colon separated list of
library names (e.g., "std:xyz").

12/20/94 -ofile_name now supported

It is now possible to specify an output file name without a space
between the "-o" and the file name.

12/20/94 EDG_DEFAULT_INCLUDE_DIRS

This new environment variable has been added.  It may be set to
a colon separated list of include file paths.  An empty path is
translated to "-I.".

11/30/94 Fix eccp problem when using -l option and templates

eccp would incorrectly use -tused when a command line like

  eccp x.c -labc

was used.  This could result in multiple definition errors or
the use of a generated instantiation when a specialization from
the library should be used.  This has been corrected.

11/4/94  Added support for Gnu binutils nm output to the prelinker

The prelinker now accepts the nm output from the Gnu binutils
nm command.  The -fgnu option is used to select this format.

10/24/94 Handling of nonlocal files by the prelinker

The prelinker and the eccp script now provide several different
options for the handling of nonlocal object files (i.e., object files
that reside in another directory).

Before this change, the prelinker would probably fail if an
instantiation were assigned to a nonlocal object file.

In the default mode, instantiations may now be assigned to nonlocal
object files.  This will result in the nonlocal file being
recompiled in the same directory as it was originally compiled in.
The prelinker has been modified to always prefer assignments to
local files.  In other words, assignments will only be made to
nonlocal files when there is no local file that can supply the
needed instantiation.

If the --prelink_local_only option is specified, instantiations
will not be assigned to nonlocal files.  Because the prelinker now
assigns instantiations to local files whenever possible, this will
result in link errors (because of missing instantiations) in cases
in which nonlocal instantiations would otherwise be done.

If the --prelink_copy_if_nonlocal option is specified, the
prelinker will, instead of assigning an instantiation to a nonlocal
file, copy the nonlocal .ii file to the local directory and
recompiled the file locally.  This mode assumes that the same
command line (except for the name of the file to be compiled) may
be used to compile the file in both the nonlocal and local
directories.

The prelinker uses single character options instead of the keyword
options now used by eccp.  The --prelink_local_only option
is translated to the -D option to edg_prelink.  The
--prelink_copy_if_nonlocal option is translated to -N.

10/24/94 Change in handling of EDG_GEN_C_SUFFIX

The handling of the EDG_GEN_C_SUFFIX variable has been expanded
to allow the entire suffix to be specified.  Formerly, only
the portion of the suffix that follows the .int could be specified.

10/20/94 Order of -L options passed to the prelinker

-L options were being passed to the prelinker in the wrong sequence.
Specifically, the system directories were incorrectly placed at the
front of the list instead of after any user specified directories.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.26, October 13, 1994

10/5/94 Generated C file suffix

The environment variable EDG_GEN_C_SUFFIX may now be used to select
an alternate suffix for the generated C file.

9/14/94 Prelinker loop when libraries are specified in the wrong order

A bug has been fixed that could cause the prelinker to loop when
library files are specified in the wrong order.  The prelinker has
been changed to suppress the instantiation of any entity for which
a definition has been seen in an archive, even if the symbol from
that archive was not actually linked in.

9/8/94  Decoding of names with leading double underscore

decode.c was changed so that it can decode names that in their original
source form begin with a double underscore, e.g., __f__Fi, which is __f(int).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.24, July 8, 1994

6/27/94 required_buffer_size parameter on decode_identifier

There is now a required_buffer_size parameter in decode_identifier,
which returns the buffer size needed.  That is useful when a buffer
overflow occurs (it tells you how big a buffer must be allocated to
try again).

6/10/94 Changes in command line handling

The eccp script has been changed to accommodate the same command line
changes that were made in the front end.

In addition to the changes described for the front end, eccp now uses
the -O option to specify that the C compiler used to compile the
generated code should be invoked with optimization requested.

The -g option no longer causes the .int.c file to be retained.
A separate option (-k or --keep_gen_c) is now available to
request that the .int.c file be preserved.

The -gn option (which was equivalent to the new -g --keep_int_c) has been
eliminated.

The --driver_debug option has been added to display, for debugging
purposes, the commands executed by the driver.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.23, May 25, 1994

4/11/94 edg_prelink displays identifiers in demangled form

edg_demangle now calls decode_identifier and displays identifiers
in decoded format.  The -m option can be used to display the
names in the old mangled format.

4/11/94 edg_prelink allows substitution in error strings

edg_prelink now provides a simple text insertion facility to
insert variable information in error messages.

4/5/94  eccp uses edg_decode to demangle the names in linker output

The eccp script has been modified to use edg_decode to demangle
names in the output of the linker.

4/5/94  Name demangler

A name demangler has been added.  The code is contained in decode.c,
and a filter program that uses the code is in edg_decode.c.

3/18/94 -L and -l options now supported by edg_prelink

The -L and -l linker options are now passed from eccp to the prelinker so
that the prelinker can include the libraries specified by the -l options
when determining which templates need to be instantiated.

3/17/94 Command line option change

The -l (don't limit recursion) option has been renamed to -r.  This has
been changed to allow the use of the -l option to specify library names.

3/1/94  Changes to facilitate error message catalogs

edg_prelink.c has been modified to simplify the task of using
a message catalog for the storage of error messages.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.22, February 26, 1994

2/21/94  Display of underlying C compiler diagnostics

Output from the underlying C compiler is bracketed by special messages
from eccp so that the source of the messages is more clear.  This
change was motivated by the fact that the C generating back end now
issues #line directives so the file name used by the C compiler in
diagnostics is now the original source file name instead of the
.int.c file name.

2/9/94   Purify option

The "-purify" option has been added to eccp.  This allows you to link
programs with purify.

1/17/94  Portability issues

edg_munch incorrectly used a char as the return value of getc.  edg_munch
and edg_prelink failed to cast the argument of isalpha to unsigned char.
These have been fixed.

edg_prelink.h no longer explicitly declares popen().  The declaration
from stdio.h is now used.

fclose was being called to close a file even when the open failed.  This
has been corrected.

1/5/94   Version of getopt routine now provided

The utility programs now provide their own version of the getopt
routine for use on systems that do not provide a getopt.

1/5/94   Temporary directory used by eccp

The eccp script now uses the environment variable TMPDIR as the temporary
directory.  If TMPDIR is not set, /tmp is used.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.21, December 21, 1993

12/16/93 Change in name of prelinker options

The nm format option for Solaris has been changed from SVR4 to Solaris
because we learned that the Solaris format is actually different from
the standard SVR4 format.

The M88K option has been renamed to SVR4 because it more closely matches
the standard SVR4 nm output.

12/14/93 Command line information in .ii file in preprocessing mode

The eccp script no longer updates the command line information in the .ii
file when invoked with options that cause the compiler to be
executed in preprocessing mode (i.e., -P, -E, -H, -M).

11/15/93 Prelinker problem with eliminated instantiation sites

Under some conditions the prelinker failed to reassign an instantiation
after the current instantiation site has been changed in such a way
that the instantiation can no longer be generated.  This has been fixed.

11/15/93 Aborting compilations that are executed by the prelinker

If a compilation is aborted while the prelinker is recompiling a file
(but before the new object file has been created) an application may
be left in a state in which simply typing "make" will not result
in the application being successfully built.  The user would need to
either remove the .o file or touch the .c file and rerun make.
This problem has been solved by having the prelinker remove the .o
file before recompiling a file.
